        "language": "english",
        "review": "I'm surprised that I'm not seeing any discourse whatsoever about how Caput Mortum can be read as an allegory about AI. There's the hubris of men trying to make people, and those \"people\" making terrible imitations of art. There's the ouroboros imagery, which has its own relevant alchemical meanings but could also tie into AI's tendency to eat its own slop to generate more slop. I don't want to go too far with spoilers, but my point is that there is so much more here than spooky atmosphere and odd controls and it's surprising that other people don't seem to be talking about it. \n\nAs you can infer from my playtime, I bounced off the gameplay and watched a walkthrough. This often happens to me with horror games. Cursed to be fascinated by the premises while put off by the gameplay. Please understand that this is a problem with me and not with the game.",
